                    {
                        "recommendationid": "51146104",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197996495980",
                            "num_reviews": 211,
                            "playtime_forever": 310,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 310,
                            "last_played": 1560118874
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The Good:\n+ Amusing opening and pre-boss cutscenes.\n+ Didn't crash during the 2.4 hours of playing (rest of the time was card idling.)\n\nThe Bad:\n- Dull combat.\n- Boring level design.\n- The non-existent options/settings aside from mute/unmute music/sound.\n- Badly designed Mouse & Keyboard controls (didn't try controller).  Can't even move if there's enemy or breakable objects within range.\n- Horribly optimized.\n- Progress isn't saved so you have to complete the entire game in one sitting.\n- Unlike the first game, no funny musical numbers during boss battles.\n\nSummary:\n- A very poor follow up to a game I liked.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1560118661,
